[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 19: 32-QAM cross.
# 32-QAM is a 6 by 6 grid without its four corners, which are the most energetic points. It carries five bits per symbol, one more than 16-QAM. Open the constellation: the cross shape, with four fewer corner points. Gray labelling cannot be perfect on a cross, so one bit error can occasionally become two. Lower the SNR in steps of 3 dB and see which points touch first.
